## 10. Job Matching Engine

Do not delegate the complete matching decision to an LLM.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    JOB[Normalized Job] --> REQ[Requirement Extraction]
    PROFILE[Candidate Profile] --> MATCH[Matching Engine]
    REQ --> MATCH

    MATCH --> D[Deterministic Signals]
    MATCH --> AI[Semantic LLM Analysis]

    D --> SCORE[Combined Match Result]
    AI --> SCORE

    SCORE --> DB[(PostgreSQL)]
```

Potential deterministic signals:

```text
Skills:       40%
Experience:   20%
Location:     15%
Role:         15%
Other:        10%
```

These percentages are configurable and should not be treated as universal truth.

LLM output should be structured:

```json
{
  "requiredSkills": [],
  "preferredSkills": [],
  "missingSkills": [],
  "relevantExperience": [],
  "semanticMatchNotes": [],
  "recommendationReason": "..."
}
```

## 11. Resume Management

Use a master resume plus modular sections.

```text
resume/
├── master.tex
├── sections/
│   ├── experience.tex
│   ├── projects.tex
│   ├── skills.tex
│   └── education.tex
└── versions/
```

## 12. AI Resume Customization

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    MASTER[Master Resume] --> PARSE[Resume Structure]
    JOB[Target Job] --> REQ[Job Requirements]
    PROFILE[Candidate Profile] --> AI[LLM Resume Planner]

    PARSE --> AI
    REQ --> AI
    PROFILE --> AI

    AI --> PLAN[Structured Resume Modification Plan]
    PLAN --> LATEX[LaTeX Generator]
    LATEX --> COMPILE[pdflatex]
    COMPILE --> PDF[Resume PDF]
    PDF --> STORAGE[(Object Storage)]
    STORAGE --> DB[(PostgreSQL)]
```

The AI should modify supported sections rather than freely rewrite the entire resume.

Example modification plan:

```json
{
  "targetRole": "Frontend Developer",
  "emphasis": [
    "React",
    "Next.js",
    "JavaScript",
    "REST APIs"
  ],
  "projectsToEmphasize": [],
  "experienceChanges": [],
  "skillsOrdering": []
}
```

## 13. Application Automation

Application automation should be a separate subsystem from job discovery.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    APPLY[Apply Action] --> URL[Application URL]
    URL --> SITE[Detect Application Site]
    SITE --> FORM[Inspect Form]
    FORM --> CLASSIFY[Classify Fields]

    PROFILE[Candidate Profile] --> MAP[Field Mapping]
    CLASSIFY --> MAP

    MAP --> ANSWER[Generate Missing Answers]
    ANSWER --> VALIDATE[Validate Data]

    VALIDATE --> REVIEW[Human Review]
    REVIEW -->|Approved| BROWSER[Playwright Worker]
    REVIEW -->|Edit| ANSWER

    BROWSER --> SUBMIT[Submit Where Permitted]
    SUBMIT --> EVENT[Application Event]
    EVENT --> DB[(PostgreSQL)]
```

## 14. Form Field Mapping

Example:

```text
First Name       -> candidate.firstName
Last Name        -> candidate.lastName
Email            -> candidate.email
Phone            -> candidate.phone
LinkedIn         -> candidate.linkedin
GitHub           -> candidate.github
Portfolio        -> candidate.portfolio
Resume           -> selected resume PDF
Experience       -> candidate.experience
Notice Period    -> candidate.noticePeriod
```

Custom questions can be passed through an LLM using only the relevant candidate profile and job context.

## 15. Human-in-the-Loop

Default workflow:

```text
Job
 ↓
Match
 ↓
Resume generated
 ↓
Application form analyzed
 ↓
Answers prepared
 ↓
Human review
 ↓
Apply
```

Do not bypass CAPTCHA, OTP, authentication challenges, anti-bot mechanisms, or website restrictions. When a site requires manual intervention, pause and hand control back to the user.

