## 28. Core Design Principles

1. APIs first, ATS endpoints second, generic scraping third.
2. Normalize every source into one canonical Job model.
3. Treat LinkedIn, Naukri, Indeed, and Glassdoor as optional source connectors rather than architectural dependencies.
4. Never write a separate scraper for every company when an ATS adapter can serve many companies.
5. Separate discovery from application automation.
6. Keep deterministic business logic outside the LLM.
7. Use LLMs for semantic extraction, reasoning, and controlled content generation.
8. Keep the master resume as the source of truth.
9. Version every generated resume.
10. Associate every application with the exact resume version used.
11. Make ingestion idempotent.
12. Use queues for long-running and failure-prone operations.
13. Keep a complete audit trail.
14. Default to human approval before final application submission.
15. Never design around bypassing CAPTCHA, OTP, authentication, anti-bot systems, or explicit site restrictions.
16. Start as a modular monolith and workers, not a premature microservice architecture.

